# Track the kaikki.org JSONL dump with Git Large File Storage (LFS).
# The file is typically 400–600 MB, well above GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# Prerequisites (one-time, per developer machine):
#   git lfs install
#
# After cloning the repo, the JSONL is replaced by a tiny LFS pointer file.
# Running `git lfs pull` (or `git lfs fetch --all`) downloads the real content.

*.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
